    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1790">

                <pb facs="1454" n="1338" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1338"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1100 K77/219b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Chargé d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 8, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received from His Excellency, Señor
                    Don Manuel E. Araujo, President of El Salvador, a handsome volume entitled:
                    “Album del Centenario” in memory of the one hundredth anniversary of the
                    beginning of the war of independence of El Salvador and the other Republics of
                    Central America.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1790-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>You will avail yourself of an early opportunity to express in person to His
                    Excellency, President Araujo, my thanks for this valuable work, so interesting
                    and instructive, which has served to recall to me with pleasure my recent visit
                    to El Salvador and the other republics of Central America.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.],</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1790-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1790-f1-content">
                <p>The “Pink Book of Salvador,” containing an account of the Secretary’s visit (File
                    No. 716.000).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
